{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Coxeter.Length"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_of_length_add_right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_of_length_add_right","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L192-L197","doc":"The right-handed mirror of `bruhatLe_of_length_add`, by transport through `⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_of_length_add","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_of_length_add","kind":"theorem","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L165-L190","doc":"**Length additivity puts the left factor below the product**: if\n`ℓ(u·w) = ℓ(u) + ℓ(w)` then `u ≤ u·w`.\n\nConcatenating reduced words for `u` and `w` gives a word of length `ℓ(u) + ℓ(w) = ℓ(u·w)`,\nso it is reduced for `u·w`, and `u`'s own word is a prefix — hence a subword.\n\nThis is the **coset-minimality bridge**, and it is what makes the row-standard\nrepresentative usable in Mathas' Prop. 3.7.  A tableau's `d` is a *distinguished* (minimal\nlength) coset representative, and `CoxeterReflectionCocycle.length_minRep_mul_wordProd'` —\nthe unconditional Bourbaki lifting lemma — supplies exactly this hypothesis for it.  So a\nstep that leaves a tableau's rows unsorted is not lost: the sorted representative sits\nbelow the raw one in Bruhat, and transitivity closes the gap.\n\nMeasured before it was proved: `d(rowsort(τ·t)) ≤ d(τ·t)` on **every** transposition of\nevery row-standard tableau of every partition of `n ≤ 6` — 2 134 710/2 134 710 at `n = 6`\n([`dipper_james_forward_step_probe.py`](../../../../../computations/hecke/dipper_james_forward_step_probe.py)). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_simple_mul_simple_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_simple_mul_simple_mul","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L152-L162","doc":"**`u ≤ w` ⇒ `sᵢ·u ≤ sᵢ·w`** when the length ascends on the **left** — the mirror of\n`bruhatLe_mul_simple_mul_simple`, obtained by transporting through `bruhatLe_inv`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_inv_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_inv_iff","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L148-L150","doc":"The `↔` form of `bruhatLe_inv`, by applying it twice. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_inv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_inv","kind":"theorem","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L126-L146","doc":"**The Bruhat order is inversion-invariant**: `u ≤ w ↔ u⁻¹ ≤ w⁻¹`.\n\nThis is the **handedness bridge**, and it is the reason this lemma is here rather than\nin a consumer.  Three separate orders on this arc multiply on opposite sides:\n\n* `Tw_mul_Tw : T_v · T_w = T_{w·v}` — the Hecke product is *anti*-multiplicative in the\n  index, forced by `orbitMap`, not a typo;\n* `TableauPerm.dOf_smul : dOf (w • t) = w * dOf t` — the tableau action puts the\n  permutation on the **left**;\n* `BruhatReflection.ReflStep v w := ∃ τ, IsReflection τ ∧ w = v * τ ∧ ℓ v < ℓ w` — the\n  reflection order steps on the **right**.\n\nA consumer that needs a left-handed statement of a right-handed lemma (or the reverse)\ntransports through this lemma rather than restating the lemma with the sides swapped.\nThe proof is the reversed word: `wordProd ω.reverse = (wordProd ω)⁻¹`, reversal preserves\nreducedness, and `List.Sublist.reverse` carries the subword across. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_mul_simple_mul_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_mul_simple_mul_simple","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L115-L124","doc":"**`u ≤ w` ⇒ `u·sᵢ ≤ w·sᵢ`** when the length ascends: extend both words by the same\nletter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_mul_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_mul_simple","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L105-L113","doc":"**`u ≤ w` ⇒ `u ≤ w·sᵢ`** when the length ascends: the same subword sits inside the\nlonger word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.isReduced_append_singleton","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.isReduced_append_singleton","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L95-L103","doc":"Appending an ascending letter to a reduced word keeps it reduced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.length_le_of_bruhatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.length_le_of_bruhatLe","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L84-L93","doc":"**Length is monotone** for the subword order: a subword is no longer than its word,\nand a reduced word has the length of its product. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.one_bruhatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.one_bruhatLe","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L79-L82","doc":"**`1 ≤ w`** — the empty subword. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.bruhatLe_refl","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L75-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.BruhatLe","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterBruhat.BruhatLe","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/CoxeterBruhat.lean#L69-L73","doc":"**The Bruhat order**, by the subword criterion: `u ≤ w` when some reduced word for\n`w` admits a subword multiplying to `u`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}